@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "SansSerif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam shadowing false

title Step-by-Step: What Happens When You Place an Order?

actor "Trader / Gateway\n(Thread 1)" as Trader
participant "SpscQueue\n(spsc_queue.hpp)" as Queue #FFF8E7
participant "OrderBook\n(order_book.hpp)" as Book #F2FBF4
participant "PriceLadders\n(bids_ / asks_)" as Ladders #EEF6FF
participant "ObjectPool & FlatHashMap\n(Memory Arena)" as Memory #FDF2F8

== Phase 1: Passing the Order Between Threads (No Locks) ==
Trader -> Queue : 1. try_push(Buy 450 shares @ $100.10)
Queue -> Book : 2. try_pop(OrderEvent)

== Phase 2: Checking if We Can Match Immediately ==
Book -> Ladders : 3. Look at asks_.back() (Lowest / Best Ask Price = $100.05)
note right: Does Buy Price ($100.10) >= Best Ask ($100.05)?\nYES! A trade happens immediately!

Book -> Ladders : 4. Match oldest order at $100.05 first (FIFO)\nFill 100 shares from #201, then 250 shares from #202
Book -> Memory : 5. Return filled OrderNodes (#201, #202) to ObjectPool\nand remove from FlatHashMap
Book -> Ladders : 6. $100.05 level is now empty -> asks_.pop_back() in O(1)!

== Phase 3: If Any Shares Remain Unfilled ==
alt Order still has remaining shares (and is a Limit Order)
    Book -> Memory : 7. Grab a pre-allocated OrderNode from ObjectPool\nand save ID -> Pointer in FlatHashMap
    Book -> Ladders : 8. Append OrderNode to the back of its PriceLevel queue
else Order is 100% filled
    Book --> Trader : Done! (Zero resting shares)
end

@enduml
